Hi there,

this is a board file submission for the WiFi / BT module found on the
Microsoft Windows Dev Kit 2023. (codename Blackrock, marketing name
"Project Volterra"). There are no new calibration data, I re-used other
already present data after an educated guess. The fitting data were from
LW_X13S.

* description for what hardware this is:

The module is described as generic "Qualcomm WCN65x We-Fi 6E Dual Band
Simultaneous (DBS) WiFiCx Network Adapter", the normal WCN6855 hw2.1.

Nov 15 07:20:58 volterra kernel: ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: BAR 0 [mem
0x30400000-0x305fffff 64bit]: assigned
Nov 15 07:20:58 volterra kernel: ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: enabling
device (0000 -> 0002)
Nov 15 07:20:58 volterra kernel: ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: MSI vectors: 32
Nov 15 07:20:58 volterra kernel: ath11k_pci 0006:01:00.0: wcn6855 hw2.1


* origin of the board file (did you create it yourself or where you
 =C2=A0 downloaded)

I used the /lib/firmware/ath11k/WCN6855/hw2.0/board-2.bin.zst available
in linux-firmware (20240318.git3b128b60-0ubuntu2.5), extracted it and
used the parts needed for this card.


* ids to be used with the board file (ATH11K_BD_IE_BOARD_NAME in ath11k)

"bus=3Dpci,vendor=3D17cb,device=3D1103,subsystem-vendor=3D17cb,subsystem-d=
evice=3D0108,qmi-chip-id=3D2,qmi-board-id=3D255,variant=3DMS_Volterra"

